-- title:
--   Dimension drop for an element avoiding the minimal primes
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is local and Noetherian, and let $x \in R$ be an element of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m} =$ `maximalIdeal R` with the property that $x \notin \mathfrak{p}$ for every $\mathfrak{p}$ in `minimalPrimes R`, that is, for every prime ideal of $R$ minimal among the primes containing $(0)$. Then, as an identity in `WithBot ℕ∞` (the value type of `ringKrullDim`), $$\dim\big(R / (x)\big) + 1 = \dim R,$$ where $(x)$ denotes `Ideal.span {x}` and both sides are Krull dimensions of commutative rings. No regularity assumption on $x$ is imposed: the hypothesis is only that $x$ lies in the maximal ideal and in none of the minimal primes, which is weaker than asking that $x$ be a non-zero-divisor. In particular, both dimensions are finite and the quotient by the principal ideal generated by such an $x$ drops the dimension by exactly one.
--
--   This is the standard fact that an element of the maximal ideal of a Noetherian local ring which avoids all minimal primes is part of a system of parameters, cutting the dimension by exactly one; it is the dimension-theoretic half of the usual induction on $\dim R$ for regular local rings. It is used here for the corresponding statement about heights of ideals in a quotient by a principal ideal, [`Ideal.height_map_quotientMk_span_singleton_add_one`](thm.html#Ideal.height_map_quotientMk_span_singleton_add_one), and in the structure result [`IsRegularLocalRing.exists_algEquiv_mvPowerSeries_quotient_span_C_sub_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair`](thm.html#IsRegularLocalRing.exists_algEquiv_mvPowerSeries_quotient_span_C_sub_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair).
